ary Request and Intent:\n   - Create a complete Claude Code hooks system with 29 lifecycle hook scripts in numbered folders under `.claude/hooks/`\n   - Each hook reads JSON from stdin, parses fields, logs with official event names, and outputs result JSON\n   - Solve cross-platform issues (Windows bash, Python detection, path handling)\n   - Bundle embedded Python environment in `.claude/localLanguage/python/` for self-contained operation\n   - Create initialization system (`.claude/init.sh`) that auto-configures on first run\n   - Create two skills: `001-testcode-python` (doc/testcode/python/ - api/ and other/) and `002-otherdoc` (doc/otherDoc/YYYY-MM-DD/ markdown archives)\n   - Skills use `InstructionsLoaded` hook in frontmatter to inject dynamic date/path info\n   - Push everything to a private GitHub repository\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Claude Code Hooks lifecycle events (29 total: SessionStart through SessionEnd)\n   - Hook configuration in `.claude/settings.json` with `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` relative paths\n   - Python embeddable package for Windows (python-3.13.9-embed-amd64.zip)\n   - Platform detection (Windows/MINGW/MSYS vs Linux vs macOS)\n   - `BASH_SOURCE[0]` vs `$0` for sourced script path resolution\n   - Windows Store Python stub detection (`$cmd -c \"pass\"` validation)\n   - Skill frontmatter with `hooks.InstructionsLoaded` for dynamic context injection\n   - `json_get.py` standalone script for reliable JSON parsing across platforms\n   - `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` for injecting info into Claude's context\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - `.claude/hooks/base.sh` - Core shared script sourced by all 29 hooks\n     - Sources platform.sh for OS detection and Python resolution\n     - Reads stdin with `cat` (not `read -d ''` which fails on Windows)\n     - Uses json_get.py for JSON field extraction\n     - Auto-extracts `hook_event_name` for `[EventName]` log prefix\n     ```bash\n     #!/bin/bash\n     HOOKS_DIR=\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks\"\n     LOG_DIR=\"$HOOKS_DIR/logs\"\n     mkdir -p \"$LOG_DIR\"\n     source \"$HOOKS_DIR/platform.sh\"\n     HOOK_INPUT=$(cat)\n     LOG_FILE=\"$LOG_DIR/$(date +%Y-%m-%d).log\"\n     json_get() {\n       local key=\"$1\"\n       if [ -z \"$HOOK_INPUT\" ]; then echo \"\"; return; fi\n       if command -v jq &>/dev/null; then\n         printf '%s' \"$HOOK_INPUT\" | jq -r \"$key\" 2>/dev/null\n         return\n       fi\n       if [ -n \"$PYTHON_CMD\" ]; then\n         printf '%s' \"$HOOK_INPUT\" | \"$PYTHON_CMD\" \"$HOOKS_DIR/json_get.py\" \"$key\" 2>>\"$LOG_FILE\"\n       else\n         echo \"\"\n       fi\n     }\n     HOOK_EVENT=$(json_get '.hook_event_name')\n     [ -z \"$HOOK_EVENT\" ] && HOOK_EVENT=\"UNKNOWN\"\n     log() {\n       echo \"[$(date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')] [$1] [$HOOK_EVENT] $2\" >> \"$LOG_FILE\"\n     }\n     hook_output() {\n       local exit_code=\"${1:-0}\"\n       local json=\"${2:-{}}\"\n       log \"INFO\" \"Output (exit=$exit_code): $json\"\n       echo \"$json\"\n       exit \"$exit_code\"\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `.claude/hooks/platform.sh` - Platform detection and Python resolution\n     ```bash\n     #!/bin/bash\n     detect_os() {\n       case \"$(uname -s)\" in\n         Linux*)   echo \"linux\" ;;\n         Darwin*)  echo \"macos\" ;;\n         MINGW*|MSYS*|CYGWIN*) echo \"windows\" ;;\n         *)        echo \"unknown\" ;;\n       esac\n     }\n     OS_TYPE=$(detect_os)\n     resolve_python() {\n       local embed\n       case \"$OS_TYPE\" in\n         windows) embed=\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/localLanguage/python/python.exe\" ;;\n         *)       embed=\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/localLanguage/python/bin/python3\" ;;\n       esac\n       if [ -x \"$embed\" ]; then echo \"$embed\"; return; fi\n       for cmd in python3 python; do\n         if command -v \"$cmd\" &>/dev/null && \"$cmd\" -c \"pass\" 2>/dev/null; then\n           echo \"$cmd\"; return\n         fi\n       done\n       echo \"\"\n     }\n     PYTHON_CMD=$(resolve_python)\n     ```\n\n   - `.claude/hooks/json_get.py` - Standalone JSON parser (stdlib only)\n     ```python\n     import sys, json\n     data = json.load(sys.stdin)\n     keys = sys.argv[1].lstrip(\".\").split(\".\")\n     v = data\n     for k in keys:\n         if isinstance(v, dict) and k in v:\n             v = v[k]\n         else:\n             v = \"\"\n             break\n     print(v if not isinstance(v, (list, dict)) else json.dumps(v, ensure_ascii=False))\n     ```\n\n   - `.claude/init.sh` - Unified initialization script (at `.claude/` root, not hooks/)\n     - Creates `doc/testcode/python/api/`, `doc/testcode/python/other/`, `doc/otherDoc/YYYY-MM-DD/`\n     - Checks `.initialized` marker to skip if already run\n     - Downloads Python embeddable for Windows if no Python found\n     - Writes marker file with OS, Python path, timestamp\n\n   - `.claude/settings.json` - Registers all 29 hooks with `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` paths\n     - All hooks use `type: \"command\"` with `bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/XX-name/base.sh\"`\n\n   - `.claude/hooks/01-session-start/base.sh` - Triggers init on first run\n     ```bash\n     [ ! -f \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/.initialized\" ] && bash \"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/init.sh\"\n     ```\n\n   - `.claude/skills/001-testcode-python/SKILL.md` - Python test scripts skill\n     - Uses `InstructionsLoaded` hook via `on_load.sh` to inject date, paths, Python path\n     - Directories: `doc/testcode/python/api/` and `doc/testcode/python/other/`\n\n   - `.claude/skills/002-otherdoc/SKILL.md` - Markdown doc archive skill\n     - Uses `InstructionsLoaded` hook via `on_load.sh` to inject date and `doc/otherDoc/YYYY-MM-DD/` path\n     - Creates date directory automatically\n\n   - `.claude/skills/001-testcode-python/scripts/on_load.sh` and `002-otherdoc/scripts/on_load.sh`\n     - Return JSON with `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` containing dynamic info\n\n   - `.gitignore` - Excludes `.cl